  "structural_change": "v15 successor of the retired flat hfd_lk_ep (13 failed routes): one ~8k-flop master for all 9 ep windows, lane gearbox 613b->512b fixed 4-in-5 format + off-die elastic RX pingpong (0az boundary), every port pin-registered, one clock root. Route-2 fix of route-1 EARLY_FAIL_HOLD (setup/hold conflict at enable-mux D pins with one 612-load select): selects replicated per 64-b slice, bypass-free SRAM leaf, macro columns facing one centre datapath channel, logic band at the COLL/SerDes faces. Route-3 fix of route-2 EARLY_FAIL_CONGESTION (12 zero-capacity M2/M4 gcells on 3 nets at the inward SRAM faces of the 47 um centre channel; abutted N-S macro pairs left no horizontal corridor): the two macro rows are separated by a 21.6 um horizontal channel (outline 434.72 x 315.36 inside the 434.72 x 515.2 window), giving the face escapes and the band->channel nets a crossing corridor. Route-4 native fix (route 3 CLOSED TT +128.49 / FF +7.69 but native launch 223.2 ps on 3 sd_tx pins, capture 212.7 ps on sd_rx[1]): sd_rx[1] (SerDes IDLE bit) loads ONE pin flop (it fed 9), the per-slice data copies and the RX gearbox beat move one edge later (+1 RX cycle at the off-die boundary, +520 flops); clk entry moved west on the S face to x 151.2-153.36 um (between tx_frame and the controls) to cut the late W-face boundary arrival.",
